<Site title="Credits & field notes">
  <article class="wrap credits"><a class="mono muted" href="/">← The arcade</a><div class="eyebrow mono">Independent by design</div><h1>BUILT FOR<br/><span>THE RIOT.</span></h1><p class="intro">One little maze. A very large corporation.<br/>An unreasonable amount of attitude.</p><section><h2>The game</h2><p>Punk-man: Escape Riot is an original browser game about scavenging, sabotage, and getting out just in time. It takes inspiration from classic maze chases and the do-it-yourself spirit of post-punk.</p><p>This first playable build has one maze, three drone personalities, three scavenged weapons, and a temporary robotic jaw. No accounts, tracking SDKs, or online leaderboards.</p></section><section><h2>Human product & agent codes</h2><p>Created by <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/andres-pi" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Andrés Pi</a>. The product direction, taste, and final decisions are human-led; Claude, Codex, Gemini, and other coding agents help explore ideas, build features, test the game, and document what we learn.</p><p>Punk Arcade is an ongoing experiment in making small, playable web experiences through human product judgment and agent-assisted code.</p></section><section><h2>Art & sound</h2><p>The maze, characters, interface, and poster use original procedural and vector artwork created for this project. Music and sound effects are original synthesized sounds generated in the browser. No external art packs, samples, or fonts are loaded.</p></section><section><h2>Built with</h2><p><a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a> powers the static site. <a href="https://phaser.io">Phaser</a> powers the game canvas and audio. Both are open-source projects distributed under the MIT license. TypeScript and plain CSS keep the rest small and direct.</p></section><section><h2>Playability notes</h2><p>Use a keyboard or the touch stick. Sound starts when you start a run and can be muted at any time. Pausing or leaving the tab freezes the run. Reduced-motion preferences disable ambient motion and shorten weapon effects.</p><p>The surrounding interface supports keyboard navigation and text status updates. The spatial canvas gameplay still requires sight; a nonvisual play mode is outside this MVP.</p></section><a class="button" href="/games/punk-man">Start a riot <span>↗</span></a></article>
</Site>
